	(descr "TE Connectivity / Schrack Power PCB Relay RT1 Inrush, part RT33K012 (1 Form A/NO, 20A UL508/16A IEC contact, AgNi90/10 'K' contact material, 12VDC/360ohm/400mW coil). PD3 replacement for K1's incumbent Omron G4A-1A-E DC12 (8.000mm coil<->contact, measured this session with the project's canonical pad-geometry kernel -- fails the 12.6mm reinforced-creepage target). Verified 2026-07-30 (docs/evidence/2026-07-30-pd3-part-selection-k1-c6-t1.md Section 1) against TE's own 'Power PCB Relay RT1 Inrush' datasheet Rev. 0415 (https://www.enika.cz/data/files/RT3_serie.pdf), drawing ref S0418-CV: 16A/1-Form-A/pinning-5mm PCB layout. TE part 2-1393240-3; DigiKey PB2347-ND, confirmed orderable/Active this session (re-verified, not re-derived from the prior document's stock check). Contact rating: RT33K row, AgNi90/10, 20A UL508 K-version / 16A IEC general rated current, 277VAC, 4000VA breaking capacity -- matches or exceeds the outgoing G4A-1A-E's 20A/12VDC declaration on the same UL508 basis. Coil: code 012 = 12VDC, 8.4V operate, 1.2V release, 360ohm+/-10%, 400mW -- DIFFERENT from the outgoing G4A-1A-E's 160ohm/75mA/900mW coil; elec/src/modules.ato's PowerInput.r_relay_drop was retuned from 39ohm to 91ohm (Yageo RSF100JB-73-91R, same 1W axial family, re-verified orderable this session) to keep this coil at ~12.0V/33.3mA from the 15V rail (15V/(360+91)=33.26mA, 33.26mA*360ohm=11.97V, 99.8% of rated -- was 112.7% of rated with the old 39ohm dropper, above IEC 61810-1's typical 110% continuous-operation ceiling). Insulation: 'Clearance/creepage between contact and coil >=10/10mm', 'Initial dielectric strength ... 5000Vrms', Material group IIIa (same internal rating class as K2/K3's already-verified sibling RT314012, same case family). VDE Cert. No. 40007571 (same certificate already investigated in docs/evidence/2026-07-29-relay-60335-1-certification-resolution.md Track B: EN/IEC 61810-1 scope only, does not itself substitute for this board's own PCB pad-to-pad measurement -- the measurement below is what actually governs). Pad geometry (position/size/drill/shape/layers) copied verbatim from KiCad 10 stock 'Relay_THT.pretty/Relay_SPST_Schrack-RT1-16A-FormA_RM5mm.kicad_mod' (re-fetched and re-read directly this session from the local KiCad footprint library, not re-derived from the datasheet drawing a second time) -- pad-for-pad identical to the geometry docs/evidence/2026-07-30-pd3-part-selection-k1-c6-t1.md Section 1.3 already measured against this exact stock file (row pitch 7.5mm, contact sub-pitch 5.04mm, coil-to-near-contact datum span 20.3mm, overall pad-field width 22.65mm; A1 rect 3x2mm, A2 oval 3x2mm, contact pads 11/14 oval 2x3mm, each with 2 physical solder holes one per row). RENUMBERED (same convention and same reason as the sibling Relay_SPDT_Schrack-RT314012.kicad_mod file): this project's Relay_SPST atopile component (elec/src/components.ato) declares a fixed pin convention -- 1=coil1, 2=coil2, 3=NO, 4=COM -- so the stock file's native 'A1'/'A2'/'11'/'14' pad names are renamed to '1'/'2'/'3'/'4' (EN50005 pin 11=COM->renamed '4', pin 14=NO->renamed '3', matching domain_manifest.yaml's power_in.bypass_relay groups coil:['1','2'] contacts:['3','4']) so every pad resolves via scripts/resync_pcb_netlist.py's exact-match path instead of positional fallback -- this part has 6 physical pad instances (A1 x1, A2 x1, contact-11 x2, contact-14 x2) against only 4 netlist-declared pins, exactly the mismatch the RT314012 footprint's own descr already flags as a positional-fallback hazard. Pad local rotation flattened from the stock file's 180 degrees to 0, verified electrically/dimensionally identical for these axis-symmetric rect/oval pads (a 180-degree rotation of a rectangle or oval about its own centre is congruent to the unrotated shape) -- same treatment RT314012 already gave the same source file. Courtyard (29.9 x 13.6mm, -2.8,-10.55 to 27.1,3.05) and silkscreen/fab graphics copied verbatim from the stock file. GOVERNING COIL<->CONTACT SEPARATION, MEASURED this session with temper_placer.core.pin_geometry.pin_world_position + temper_placer.core.pad_geometry.pad_pair_distance (the same canonical, rotation-and-side-aware kernel PR #1146/#1152 used, NOT a datasheet-drawing hand computation): pad '1' (coil1, local (0,0), rect 3x2) <-> pad '4' (COM, local (20.3,0), oval 2x3): 17.8000mm edge-to-edge -- clears the 12.6mm PD3 reinforced-creepage target with +5.2mm margin. See docs/evidence/ for this session's full re-verification writeup. No 3D model reference carried over (same reason as RT314012: the stock file's own model points at a sibling RT2/DPDT step file, unverified for this specific part -- omitted rather than propagated).")
